# Byte-exact pinned upstream guide files: creative_skills.py SHA-256-checks
# them at runtime. git's line-ending conversion (autocrlf=true is the default
# Windows install) rewrote these LF files to CRLF on checkout, changing every
# hash and making the official skill feature fail forever on Windows clones.
# -text tells git to never touch these bytes.
prompt_guides/official_minimax/** -text
prompt_guides/official_minimax/**/* -text
